{"path":"experimental/ranges/concepts/Same","title":"std::experimental::ranges::Same","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::ranges::</span>Same","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/ranges/concepts/Same","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"The concept Same<T, U> is satisfied if and only if T and U denote the same type.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/experimental/ranges/concepts\">&lt;experimental/ranges/concepts&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-ranges\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T, <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> U <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>concept <span class=\"kw4\">bool</span> Same <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_same\"><span class=\"kw591\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_same</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// see below</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-ranges-ts t-mark-ts\">(ranges TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The concept <code>Same&lt;T, U&gt;</code> is satisfied if and only if <code>T</code> and <code>U</code> denote the same type.\n</p><p>Despite being specified using it, there need not be any subsumption relationship between <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">Same<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_same\"><span class=\"kw591\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_same</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">value</span></span></code>.\n</p><p>For the purposes of constraint checking, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">Same<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T, U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> implies <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">Same<span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U, T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The additional requirement on constraint checking differentiates <code>Same</code> from <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_same\">std::is_same</a></span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_same\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_same</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if two types are the same  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/ranges","title":"Extensions for ranges"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::ranges::Same","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. The concept Same<T, U> is satisfied if and only if T and U denote the same type."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The additional requirement on constraint checking differentiates Same from std::is_same."},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"is_same","note":"checks if two types are the same"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":89,"codeBlockCount":0}
